  "details": "Some VRChat communities currently have at least 100 to 500 members banned. When users appeal these bans, it is difficult for moderators to manage the appeal process due to significant limitations in the ban feature.\n\nWhen a moderator initially bans a user, they are briefly presented with an option to unban them before navigating away from that screen.\n\nHowever, once the moderator closes that screen, there is no way to unban the user by looking them up in the research bar (or search function), for example. If a moderator attempts to search for the banned user and clicks the 'Ban' button, the system simply confirms the user is \"already banned.\" There is no accessible unban option displayed at this point.\n\nThe current ban function within the moderation tools needs to be fixed so that moderators can look up banned users directly through the search/research bar and unban them. This change would be significant. It would eliminate the current need to search through the separate, web-based ban list to process appeals, making the moderation workflow much more efficient for VRChat communities on the platform.\n\nFrom,\n\nKitsune.",
